# Sigma Governance — Cursor Bridge

This project uses the Sigma governance CLI for structured lifecycle management.

Refer to `SIGMA_README.md` at the project root for the full governance protocol.

## Quick Reference

| What you need | How to get it |
|---|---|
| Current project state | Run `sigma project status` in terminal |
| Session orientation | Run `sigma session bootstrap` in terminal |
| When stuck or lost | Run `sigma project status` and read the "Next Valid Operations" list |

## Rules for AI Roles

- Do not edit `Sigma/progress-v<N>.json` directly — all state changes go through `sigma` CLI commands
- Do not lock artifacts without explicit Director authorization
- When a gate is blocked, surface the blocker clearly before proposing work

## Artifact Reference

| Human label | Artifact code | State flow |
|---|---|---|
| Intent Doc | DIR-INTENT | DRAFT → RATIFIED |
| Plan Doc | FMN-PLAN | DRAFT → LOCKED |
| Execution Evidence | DEV-EXEC | DRAFT → BUILDING → TESTING → COMPLETED → LOCKED |
| Closure Doc | DIR-CLOSE | DRAFT → LOCKED |
| Roadmap Doc | ROADMAP | DRAFT → LOCKED (optional) |

## Gate Reference

| Gate | Requires | Unlocks |
|---|---|---|
| Gate 1 | DIR-INTENT RATIFIED | `sigma plan new` |
| Gate 2 | FMN-PLAN LOCKED | `sigma exec new` |
| Gate 3 | DEV-EXEC LOCKED + full evidence chain | `sigma close new` |
